From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t41: handle i2c client creation errors

i2c_new_client_device() returns an ERR_PTR on failure, not NULL. The
recovered T41 flow checks only for NULL and then dereferences
client->dev.driver, so when the DT sensor driver already owns the address
(EBUSY) the kernel panics on the ERR_PTR:

  gc8613 0-0031: Failed to register i2c client gc8613 at 0x31 (-16)
  BadVA: 00000048
  epc: ... <8c420058>  lw v0,0x58(v0)

Match the T31 fix: treat ERR_PTR as a failed registration, normalize it
to NULL so the cleanup path does not call i2c_unregister_device() on an
error pointer.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/driver/t41/tx_isp_t41_recovered.c
+++ b/driver/t41/tx_isp_t41_recovered.c
@@ -15102,7 +15102,11 @@
 	}
 
 	client = private_i2c_new_device(adapter, info);
-	if (!client || !client->dev.driver)
+	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(client)) {
+		client = NULL;
+		goto error;
+	}
+	if (!client->dev.driver)
 		goto error;
 
 	owner = client->dev.driver->owner;
